<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="060" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>ISS-003: resolve the sprk_event rows stranded in Draft</title>
    <phase>6 Do lane and Briefing fold-in</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>blocked</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Data correctness in another domain that this project depends on; the Do lane under-reports without it.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Diagnosis is already recorded; the fix is scoped.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,dataverse,bug</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Resolve the 48 sprk_event rows stranded in Draft, so the Do lane does not silently under-report.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer.</role>
  <goal>No task created by the platform is invisible to the surface that exists to surface it.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>TaskActionCore did not set statuscode Open, so every task the platform created was invisible to the briefing. 48 rows remain stranded in Draft (re-measured live 2026-10-02; was 49). The code fix landed in PR #1032; the DATA remains stranded. A due-date rule is only as good as the task data under it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">Dataverse: sprk_event rows (spaarkedev1)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: this is a DATA remediation, not a code change. The code fix (TaskActionCore setting statuscode Open) already landed in PR #1032 and is in master.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: a domain owner must review the PR #1032 semantics, in particular TaskActionCore now setting statuscode Open for EVERY consumer. Do not widen that behaviour here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: re-count before and after. The number was 49 then 48; quoting a stale count is the same error class as quoting a stale publish-size baseline.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: any test this task adds that asserts a Dataverse column list, entity name or option-set value must be paired with something touching the real schema. A consistently throwing path is a defect to diagnose, never noise to tolerate.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Data remediation</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/schema-draft.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/security-roles.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above before touching code.</step>
    <step order="1">Re-count the stranded rows and record the current number.</step>
    <step order="2">Determine which of them SHOULD be Open versus legitimately Draft; do not blanket-update.</step>
    <step order="3">Update the ones that should be Open, recording the ids.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-count and confirm the remainder is explained.</step>
    <step order="5">Close GitHub issue 1050 with the before and after counts.</step>
    <step order="6">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task to the completed marker, AND set this POML status element to completed. Both, or scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 fails the next push.</step>
    <step order="7">Record any deviation from this POML in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If some stranded rows cannot be classified as either legitimately Draft or wrongly Draft, STOP and escalate to the communication-intelligence domain owner rather than blanket-updating. A blanket update would make 48 tasks suddenly appear in users briefings.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="data">Dataverse: corrected sprk_event rows</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the stranded rows, when re-counted after the fix, then the remaining count is zero or every remainder is explained in writing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the corrected rows, when the briefing collector runs, then they are visible to it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no row was updated that was legitimately Draft.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GitHub issue 1050 is closed with before and after counts.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md section 8.1 step 4 dependency. ISS-003. This BLOCKS the Do lane: shipping the lane first makes it under-report silently.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
  <completion>
    <status>blocked-escalated</status>
    <date>2026-10-07</date>
    <summary>Escalation trigger fired at step 2; NO data was changed. Live re-count (spaarkedev1): Draft 49 (not 48), Open 22, Completed 7, Cancelled 1. All 49 Draft rows were created by the same single user (1d02f31c-...), 0 have sprk_regardingcommunication, so the issue-1050 classifier (createdby + regardingcommunication) does not separate system-generated from human-authored. Names are mixed: generic 'Task' rows (Feb 2026), 'Assign Work', 'Analysis AI review', 'Event', and obvious manual test rows ('Task 5 7/9/2026', 'Test new event'). Of these only the Task-type rows could be argued Open; the rest are Event/untyped. Note IsOpenWork already counts Draft, so the Do lane does not under-report these; only the briefing's statuscode=Open filter misses them.</summary>
    <needs>Owner / communication-intelligence domain owner decision on the classification rule and approval of any bulk update (count and plan reported to the main session). Issue 1050 left open; TASK-INDEX untouched.</needs>
  </completion>
</task>
